        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0764" n="674" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg674"/>

                <head>No. 302.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Peirce to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-02-26"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 26, 1875</date>.
                        (Received March 29.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 317.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On Saturday the 20th instant, His Majesty
                    the King addressed the people, who filled to repletion the large Congregational
                    church in <pb facs="0765" n="675" xml:id="pg675"/> Honolulu, and gave a brief
                    narrative of the incidents of his late tour to the United States, and it was
                    spoken in both the English and Hawaiian languages.</p>
                <p>A printed copy of the address, published in the Hawaiian Gazette of the 24th
                    instant, is herewith inclosed. It is desirable that you should give it an
                    attentive perusal, particularly as the address was composed by His Majesty, and
                    presents the impressions and observations derived from his visit to the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>The resolution of thanks to the Government of the United States, which was
                    unanimously passed by the people assembled on the above occasion, was ordered by
                    the. King to be printed on satin and forwarded to the President of the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>With great respect, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HENRY A. PEIRCE.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d306-a1.xml" xpointer="d306-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
